{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades","id":1333013,"title":"Firedust Grenades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-28T12:17:50-07:00","id":1333013,"title":"Firedust Grenades","content":"So I just read the writeup for bats in ex3, and their guano mixed with red jade dust can make firedust grenades. First of all, good job on the fireball reagent nod. Otherwise though, are there stats for firedust grenades anywhere? I recall there was a discussion a while ago about how to balance them, but I don't think there was any good conclusion to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T12:39:14-07:00","id":1333015,"title":"","content":"I suspect that it had to do more with the original reference for why it was a reagent for the fireball spell, as guano was often used as a source of saltpeter for pre-industrial gunpowder production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T13:15:45-07:00","id":1333020,"title":"","content":"Oh right...duh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T13:16:45-07:00","id":1333021,"title":"","content":"Unofficially, someone wrote <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278078/The-Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-5\" target=\"_blank\">a martial art for grenades</a> which includes rules for grenades :<br /> <br /> -Grenades are a medium Thrown weapon that cost 4 dots of resource to afford reliably (3 dots in the South)<br /> -Withering attacks damage everyone in close range of the target. You only get initiative from the primary target, but crashing a secondary target award 1ini. +2 post-soak damage against battlegroups.<br /> -Decisive attacks split initiative evenly, +2 attack bonus against battlegroups.<br /> -Botching a grenade toss detonates the grenade on you, causing an environmental hazard within close range of you.<br /> -Can perform Feats of Demolition up to Strength 5<br /> <br /> So in this write-up they're pretty strong and mostly balanced by their cost and the danger of using them in close quarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T13:20:12-07:00","id":1333024,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I'd just make them Heavy Thrown weapons with the flame tag. That's the simplest way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T14:16:34-07:00","id":1333029,"title":"","content":"The 2E stats are in Scroll of Kings, right?<br /> <br /> I think Firedust Grenades are closer to: Medium weapon, Thrown (Short), Lethal, Flame, Mounted, Special (all characters within Close range of the target lose 1 Initiative which the attacker does not gain (Uniform); Battlegroups don't add Size to Soak and take one additional level of damage on Decisive attacks), Balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-29-2019, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T14:19:36-07:00","id":1333030,"title":"","content":"I think I\u2019d go for having them be a gambit that makes a bonfire hazard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T16:40:32-07:00","id":1333045,"title":"","content":"Didn't the Adversaries of the Righteous write-up for that gang of swamp people with the trained crocodiles include a sidebar on a gambit for using grenades in combat?<br /> <br /> Which is to say, I know that sidebar definitely exists, and its in one of the Adversaries write-ups, was it that one specifically?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly a little bit dubious about alchemy as a Craft and particularly about that recipe for manufacturing firedust, but I can kind of square it if I imagine that jade is difficult enough to acquire under circumstances where you could grind it for extra powder to be used in an ingredient for something like firedust (I imagine it's something you do almost only when there's no recourse for just being the natural stuff), and that alchemy as a rule requires the inclusion of something rare and mystical to get your desired transmutation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope, not about grenades, just generally igniting some explosive material in the vicinity. Dummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-28-2019, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T17:37:49-07:00","id":1333047,"title":"","content":"Hmmm yeah this is a tough one. Considering the only real cost to them is either money or being/having access to an alchemist in the party I'm not sure I feel totally comfortable giving them an AoE attack. I think that as a mortal game or something like that you could get away with it, but once charms start getting involved it might get out of control. For one they combo with any simple type charm, so Thousand Razor Wind becomes a charm that lets you throw out 5-7 AoE attacks in a single action.<br /> <br /> Making it a medium/heavy weapon that unlocks a special gambit though would be a lot easier to balance. Maybe like difficulty 3-4 for a one time bonfire? That's still pretty good considering heavy ranged weapons are strictly better than lighter ones, not counting tags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T19:25:54-07:00","id":1333055,"title":"","content":"I agree that a half-dozen AoEs would break things, but making grenades into a single target weapon feels like removing a vital element of flavor for the sake of balance. Some ideas :<br /> <br /> A) the simplest, laziest fix : grenades cannot do withering attacks.<br /> <br /> B) death of mortals fix : grenades deal their AoE with a hazard roll (the hazard from a Withering Attack could lower ini by a fixed amount instead of damaging health). So mortals still get chewed alive by the AoE but exalts can laugh off all these easy hazard rolls. This is the fix I favor myself.<br /> <br /> C) limited scaling fix : add a rule that grenade AoE doesn't stack within the same Tick. So in the 7 attacks scenario you could land 7 attacks but the AoE of all combined attacks would not hit each enemy more than once. Unless fighting like 12 distinct combatants it should prevent things from getting out of control. If needed can also add that an enemy hit by a direct hit cannot take AoE damage from the other grenades in the same attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-28-2019, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T20:38:02-07:00","id":1333064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades?p=1333055#post1333055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B) death of mortals fix : grenades deal their AoE with a hazard roll (the hazard from a Withering Attack could lower ini by a fixed amount instead of damaging health). So mortals still get chewed alive by the AoE but exalts can laugh off all these easy hazard rolls. This is the fix I favor myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>A solution something like that is probably the best, since most of the crazy insane BS you can do comes from mixing charms into the thing, and not a lot of charms enhance a secondary hazard effect on your attacks. It also gets around the idea that you're blanketing a huge number of onslaugtht penalties on multiple targets.<br /> <br /> The multiattack thing still kind of gets me though if it lets you template down a half dozen area hazards in a single action. I'm trying really hard to make my games not devolve into meaningless a backdrop of non-exalts against the only things in the setting that ever matter which are exalts. Even then while a lot of exalts do have resistance excellencies, not all do, and even the ones that have them don't want to be spending 15 motes in a single defense. If the difficulty was only 1-2 that might be okay, although it might get a bit tedious to roll those out all the time, but if you start getting into the 4-5 range even dedicated exalts don't have a good chance of making all five saves.<br /> <br /> Maybe combined with the limited scaling it could work, like it applies a one-time hazard regardless of how many attacks you make with it. It would still be really powerful but balanced with more frequent ammunition checks I think it could work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T02:58:39-07:00","id":1333080,"title":"","content":"What if the splash only dealt 1 Initiative damage (automatically, not rolled) which the attacker didn't gain? That'd cut back rolls, and if you're blowing motes and one-use grenades to attack seven times AND your foes are standing within Close of each other AND at Short from you, then you deserve to do 7i to them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:45:30-07:00","id":1333101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades?p=1333080#post1333080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the splash only dealt 1 Initiative damage (automatically, not rolled) which the attacker didn't gain? That'd cut back rolls, and if you're blowing motes and one-use grenades to attack seven times AND your foes are standing within Close of each other AND at Short from you, then you deserve to do 7i to them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think that would work. You\u2019re probably only carrying enough grenades to do that once, it hits your allies so you won\u2019t be doing it all the time, it doesn\u2019t interact with most charms, and it doesn\u2019t have a huge amount of rolling. There are times when you\u2019d want it, but it doesn\u2019t turn every non-grenade option into a trap either. I\u2019d still have to make some case by case rulings, no Persistent Hornet Attack for example. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not insurmountable the other way either. If my players encounter somebody like that I don\u2019t have to tell everyone without 8 dice to their hazard resistance roll and an excellency to hand over their character sheet as they\u2019re blown to pieces by a half dozen simultaneous bonfires. <br /> <br /> <br /> The only other way I can see it working in a way that keeps the feel of a grenade is if you don\u2019t treat it like a weapon at all. No attack roll, just a combat action to use the grenade and it creates a one time hazard at short range, maybe weaker than a bonfire but they also suffer an onslaught penalty as though they\u2019d been attacked. It\u2019s still really useful in that case, you\u2019re getting a moteless ranged AoE attack that does direct decisive damage. That puts them about on par with poisons, which are also monetarily expensive single use items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:40:23-07:00","id":1342513,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that most of what made Firedust Grenades a problem in Scroll of Kings were issues with applying the environmental hazard rules in combat, they've been fixed by the new edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T02:16:46-07:00","id":1342667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades?p=1342513#post1342513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that most of what made Firedust Grenades a problem in Scroll of Kings were issues with applying the environmental hazard rules in combat, they've been fixed by the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone whose knowledge of Second Edition is very superficial. may I ask what where the issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T08:37:47-07:00","id":1342715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades?p=1342667#post1342667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone whose knowledge of Second Edition is very superficial. may I ask what where the issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>2E made you take Bashing, Lethal or Aggravated damage from a hazard every interval. The interval could be every tick or every action, but was probably every minute, every hour or every day. If you were only taking environmental damage every hour, you weren't taking damage in combat.<br /> <br /> You could also resist elemental damage pretty trivially. Meaning you can just shrug it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-21-2019, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:46:17-07:00","id":1342800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333013-firedust-grenades?p=1342667#post1342667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone whose knowledge of Second Edition is very superficial. may I ask what where the issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation in Scroll of Kings-<br /> - Hazards were only resisted with (Stamina + Resistance) a pool a lot of characters didn't max out unless they were beefcakes or combat optimised.<br /> -Meeting the difficulty of a Hazard or Poison that dealt lethal damage didn't prevent damage, it just downgraded its severity to bashing damage unless you rolled double. Which, coupled with the former point made them something of a wonder weapon.<br /> -For most of 2nd edition if you attacked someone by any vector you were entitled to (essence) minumum damage unless your damage was lower to begin with. This, coupled with the fact that most splats lacked combat healing, made downgrading that damage to bashing even more useless.<br /> -Grenades were noted as being fragile and could go off if you suffered knockdown/knockback - but the nature of 2e combat was that if someone was hitting you then something was probably very wrong.<br /> <br /> They annoyed me for having this contradictory half-verisimilitude where you couldn't dodge the explosion without a perfect defence, cos that's unrealistic. But your armour didn't help protect against them only your natural fortitude, because... reasons? I guess?<br /> <br /> <br /> If this was ported over to Third edition-<br /> -Hazards can be resisted with a variety of dice pools including (Dexterity + Dodge).<br /> -They have a fixed difficulty which makes them much easier to shrug off.<br /> -Minimum damage has been 1 since the 2.5 errata.<br /> - The Smashing tag means you're way more likely to get knocked around and have your grenades blow up in your face.<br /> -Trying to deal direct damage like this instead of building initiative via withering damage has obvious downsides. Tactically you'd be in the same boat as the sorcerer who wants to stand back and blast away with spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-21-2019, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}